.TH TAI64N 1 "April 2026" "go-libtai" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tai64n \- read stdin and prepend TAI64N timestamps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tai64n
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tai64n
reads standard input and prepends each line with a TAI64N timestamp 
(hexadecimal TAI64 seconds followed by nanoseconds, preceded by @).
It is intended for high-precision log timestamping.
.PP
Each line is printed with the timestamp followed by a single space.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tai_now (1),
.BR taia_now (1)
.SH AUTHOR
This tool is part of go-libtai, a Go implementation of D. J. Bernstein's 
libtai.
.SH NOTES
The TAI64N format and its specifications were originally established by 
D. J. Bernstein in his libtai library (https://cr.yp.to/libtai.html).
.PP
This tool is a Go reimplementation of DJB's tai64n(1) tool.
